.TH GLADOS-REPL 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
glados\-repl \- interactive Read-Eval-Print Loop for Quant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glados\-repl
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glados\-repl
is an interactive shell for the Quant language. Each expression or
statement typed at the prompt is compiled and executed immediately, with
the result printed to stdout. Multiline input is supported: an open brace
or unclosed expression causes the prompt to switch to a continuation
indicator until the block is closed.
.PP
The REPL shares the full compiler and VM pipeline with
.BR glados (1),
so all language features, imports, and standard library modules are
available.
.SH REPL COMMANDS
The following dot-prefixed commands are available at the prompt:
.TP
.B :load \fIFILE\fR
Compile and load \fIFILE\fR into the current session. All top-level
declarations become available at the prompt.
.TP
.B :run
Re-execute the \fBmain\fR function if one is defined in the loaded file.
.TP
.B :env
Print all names currently in scope together with their types.
.TP
.B :reset
Clear the session state: all loaded declarations and definitions are
removed and the session starts fresh.
.TP
.B :quit
Exit the REPL. Ctrl-D also works.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
Tab completion
Function names, variable names, and keywords are completed on Tab.
.TP
History
Command history is preserved across sessions.
.TP
Multiline input
Opening a block with \fB{\fR suspends evaluation until the block is closed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUANT_STDLIB
Path to the Quant standard library used when resolving \fBimport\fR
statements typed at the prompt.
